fuse|REVIEW: The 4600 record supports the burning-cord noun only, not an electrical device or verb. The museum-style diagram example gives no operating instructions; specialist boundary remains for owner review.
medication|PASS: Medicine collectively is usually uncountable, while different medications are countable. An appointment list supplies no dosage or treatment advice; thuốc đang dùng preserves the possession context naturally.
ring|PASS: Four source ordinals remain separate: jewellery, bell sound, British telephone verb and circle. Rang/rung morphology, telephone transitivity and the grandfather possessive are checked independently.
sceptical|PASS: Qualified doubt and the evidence-based change of view align in both languages. British spelling is retained as the key; the American variant is grammar guidance, not a fabricated second lexical identity.
weigh|PASS: Stative weight and active measurement retain distinct valency and ordinals. The comparative parcel example does not invent an amount; the flour example is an ordinary transitive measurement construction.
